**Goal** — Remove the `autoMigrateGeneratedContent` call from `setupRun` and its `_runSetupDeps` member so a run no longer moves in-repo `.nax/` content.

**Motivation** — The auto-migration matches live in-repo data that current nax writes and reads (`.nax/features/<f>/sessions/`, `status.json`, `stories/<s>/context-manifest-*.json`), renames it into `~/.nax/<project>/features/...`, throws `MIGRATE_CONFLICT` on the first collision and logs `warn "Auto-migration failed — continuing without migration"`; a successful move takes live data away from the in-repo readers.

**Approach** — `_runSetupDeps` (`packages/nax/src/execution/lifecycle/run-setup.ts`). Baseline: contains `autoMigrateGeneratedContent(workdir)`, which lazily imports and calls `autoMigrateGeneratedContent` from `@/commands`. Target: that member is removed. `setupRun` no longer calls anything between priming the status writer and claiming the project identity. Nothing replaces the member or the call: `setupRun` goes straight from priming the status writer to claiming the project identity. Delete `packages/nax/test/unit/execution/lifecycle/run-setup-auto-migrate.test.ts`; it pins that `setupRun` calls `_runSetupDeps.autoMigrateGeneratedContent` exactly once, which is the call this story removes. The replacing invariant, in the new `run-setup-no-migration.test.ts`, is that `setupRun` leaves in-repo feature artifacts in place. Copy the local `captureLogs` helper from `packages/nax/test/integration/commands/migrate-tracked-candidates.test.ts` into the new test, because US-003 deletes that file.

**Scope** — In: `run-setup.ts` seam removal, deletion of the auto-migrate unit test, the new no-migration test. Out: anything in `src/commands/migrate.ts`, `src/commands/index.ts`, `bin/nax.ts` (US-002/US-003); moving any in-repo `.nax/features/<f>/` content anywhere (it stays where nax reads it); cleaning up `~/.nax/<project>/features/*/sessions/` directories an earlier auto-migration left behind; `setupRun` only reads `projectOutputDir`, `validateProjectName`, `readProjectIdentity` and `writeProjectIdentity`.

**Interface**
```typescript
// packages/nax/src/execution/lifecycle/run-setup.ts
// Baseline: _runSetupDeps contains autoMigrateGeneratedContent(workdir)
// Target: that member is removed; setupRun(options: RunSetupOptions) is otherwise unchanged
```

**Goal** — Make `migrateCommand` throw `MIGRATE_NO_MODE` when neither `reclaim` nor `merge` is set, remove the generated-content move branch and `--dry-run`, and update the `migrate` command description.

**Motivation** — The generated-content migration is finished work and harmful on live in-repo data; `nax migrate --reclaim` and `--merge` are collision recovery, not migrations, and must stay.

**Approach** — `MigrateOptions` (`packages/nax/src/commands/migrate.ts`). Baseline: `{ workdir: string; dryRun?: boolean; reclaim?: string; merge?: string }`. Target: `{ workdir: string; reclaim?: string; merge?: string }`. `migrateCommand(options: MigrateOptions): Promise<void>` baseline: `--reclaim` branch, then `--merge` branch, then the generated-content move (config read, `detectGeneratedContent`, `partitionTrackedCandidates`, dry-run report, `MIGRATE_CONFLICT` / `MIGRATE_CROSS_FS` / `MIGRATE_MOVE_FAILED`, and the `.migrated-from` marker). Target: the `--reclaim` branch, then the `--merge` branch, both unchanged and in that order. With neither flag set, it throws `NaxError` with code `MIGRATE_NO_MODE`, message `nax migrate needs --reclaim <name> or --merge <name>`, and context `{ stage: "migrate", workdir }`. It touches no file (no config read, no mkdir, no rename). Pattern to follow: the `--reclaim` and `--merge` branches already validate their input and throw a `NaxError` with a `MIGRATE_*` code and a `stage: "migrate"` context. The `migrate` command definition (`packages/nax/bin/nax.ts`, around line 400): baseline options `-d/--dir`, `--dry-run`, `--reclaim <name>`, `--merge <name>`, passing `dryRun` to `migrateCommand`. Target: options `-d/--dir`, `--reclaim <name>`, `--merge <name>`; description `Recover a project-name collision: --reclaim or --merge`. The existing catch prints `Error: <message>` in red and exits 1, so a `MIGRATE_NO_MODE` rejection exits 1 with the usage message. CLI behaviour: `nax migrate --reclaim <name>` and `--merge <name>` unchanged; `nax migrate` (neither flag) exits 1 with stderr `Error: nax migrate needs --reclaim <name> or --merge <name>`; `nax migrate --dry-run` exits 1 with commander's `error: unknown option '--dry-run'`. Tests: remove the `describe("migrateCommand — full migration flow")` block from `test/unit/commands/migrate.test.ts` (its cases pin `MIGRATE_NO_CONFIG`, `MIGRATE_CONFIG_READ_FAILED`, "nothing to migrate", dry-run, the move with its `.migrated-from` marker, the basename project key, `MIGRATE_CONFLICT` and `MIGRATE_MOVE_FAILED`) and the now-unused `chmod` import; keep the `mkdir` import (the `detectGeneratedContent` block still uses it until US-003) and keep the `--reclaim`/`--merge` describe blocks unchanged. Remove the `describe("US-003 migrateCommand")` block from `test/integration/commands/migrate-tracked-candidates.test.ts`; other describe blocks stay until US-003. The replacing invariant is the `MIGRATE_NO_MODE` rejection. Regenerate `packages/nax/scripts/baselines/complexity-baseline.json` with `bun run check:complexity:update` (removing the move branch lowers `migrateCommand` below its recorded 41; the ratchet fails a stale row). The CLI ACs spawn `bun bin/nax.ts`; this is a deliberate exception to the "Spawning full `nax` process in tests" rule in `.nax/rules/forbidden-patterns-tests.md`, because the command is defined inline in `bin/nax.ts` and cannot be imported, and `test/unit/cli/trust.test.ts` already spawns the CLI this way. Every spawn sets `NAX_GLOBAL_CONFIG_DIR` to a temp dir so no spawn reaches the real `~/.nax`.

**Scope** — In: `migrateCommand` mode check and removal of the move branch, `MigrateOptions.dryRun`, `bin/nax.ts` migrate definition, test removals, new `migrate-cli.test.ts`, complexity baseline regeneration. Out: deleting `GENERATED_NAMES`, `GENERATED_FEATURE_SUBNAMES`, `detectGeneratedContent`, `partitionTrackedCandidates`, `autoMigrateGeneratedContent`, `MigrateCandidate`, `_gitDeps` re-export, and the `commands/index.ts` exports (US-003); `run-setup.ts` (US-001); changing `--reclaim`/`--merge` behaviour.

**Interface**
```typescript
// packages/nax/src/commands/migrate.ts
export interface MigrateOptions {
  workdir: string;
  reclaim?: string;
  merge?: string;
}
export function migrateCommand(options: MigrateOptions): Promise<void>;
// neither reclaim nor merge -> throws NaxError(
//   "nax migrate needs --reclaim <name> or --merge <name>",
//   "MIGRATE_NO_MODE", { stage: "migrate", workdir })
```

**Goal** — Delete the now-unreferenced generated-content migration helpers, their exports, their tests, and update the docs.

**Motivation** — With the move branch and the run-setup call gone, the helpers are dead code that still matches live in-repo data and must not be re-wired.

**Approach** — Deletion only. Remove `GENERATED_NAMES`, `GENERATED_FEATURE_SUBNAMES`, `detectGeneratedContent`, `partitionTrackedCandidates`, `autoMigrateGeneratedContent`, `MigrateCandidate` and the `_gitDeps` re-export from `packages/nax/src/commands/migrate.ts`. No source file outside `migrate.ts` and `commands/index.ts` imports any of them. Once they are gone, `migrate.ts` no longer uses its `gitWithTimeout`, `readdir`, `getSafeLogger` or `projectOutputDir` imports, and those are removed; `mkdir` and `rename` stay, because `--reclaim` uses them (`lint:biome` runs first in `check:all` and rejects unused imports). Rewrite the module doc comment to describe project-name collision recovery. `packages/nax/src/commands/index.ts`: remove the `autoMigrateGeneratedContent`, `detectGeneratedContent` and `partitionTrackedCandidates` exports and the `MigrateCandidate` type export; `migrateCommand` and `MigrateOptions` stay (the target exports are `migrateCommand` and the type `MigrateOptions` only). Delete `packages/nax/test/integration/commands/migrate-tracked-candidates.test.ts` (every remaining case exercises the deleted functions; nothing replaces it). In `packages/nax/test/unit/commands/migrate.test.ts` remove the `describe("detectGeneratedContent")` block, its import and the `mkdir` import (nothing else in the file uses `mkdir`); the `--reclaim` and `--merge` blocks and the US-002 `MIGRATE_NO_MODE` cases stay. Regenerate `packages/nax/scripts/baselines/complexity-baseline.json` with `bun run check:complexity:update` (deleting `detectGeneratedContent`, recorded at 54, leaves a stale row; the row is gone if no function in the file is over the limit). Docs: `docs/guides/cli-reference.md` — the `nax migrate` section drops the `nax migrate --dry-run` example and the `--dry-run` flag-table row, describes project-name collision recovery only, and keeps the `--reclaim` and `--merge` examples. `packages/nax/README.md` — the `nax migrate` table row becomes "Recover a project-name collision: `--reclaim <name>` or `--merge <name>`". `docs/architecture/subsystems.md` line ~1745 — replace the `migrateCommand(opts)` / `detectGeneratedContent()` legacy-format description with: `migrateCommand` handles `--reclaim` / `--merge` project-identity collision recovery only. `scripts/check-worktree-id-ssot.ts` keeps `src/commands/migrate.ts` in `ALLOWED_FILES` and needs no change. Verification: `bun run typecheck` and `bun run check:all` in `packages/nax`; the compiler rejects any remaining reference to a removed symbol and the complexity ratchet rejects a stale `src/commands/migrate.ts` row.

**Scope** — In: symbol deletion in `migrate.ts` and `commands/index.ts`, test deletions, baseline regeneration, three doc edits. Out: the `MIGRATE_NO_MODE` behaviour, `bin/nax.ts` and the `run-setup.ts` seam (US-001/US-002); any change to the `--reclaim` / `--merge` branches; the tracked `.nax/features/run-hygiene-bugs/.nax-acceptance.test.ts` (manual follow-up); rewriting historical design documents under `docs/specs/`; other "migrate" code (`nax rules migrate`, `config/migrations`, `pb-004-migration`, `default-agent-migration`).

**Interface**
```typescript
// packages/nax/src/commands/index.ts (target exports from migrate)
export { migrateCommand } from "./migrate";
export type { MigrateOptions } from "./migrate";
```
